 "transcript": "Today at 10.15, Pacific Time, the Idaho Supreme Court hears Lori Vallo-Daybell's appeal. First, the victims, her son, Seven, her daughter, Sixteen, and Tammy Daybell, 49. In 2023, a jury convicted her of first-degree murder in the deaths of her son and daughter. It also convicted her of conspiring to murder Tammy Daybell. She is serving life without parole. Today is a review, not a new trial. No witnesses testify. Her attorneys say the judge wrongly removed the attorney she hired, and that she was denied a speedy trial. The state asks the court to keep her convictions in place. The justices rule later, in writing. Until then, her convictions stand. Court dates and sources, CassianCreed.com Court Calendar.",
